    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0940" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1834</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Oral Statement by the Counselor of Embassy in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dooman</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Accompanying Aide-mémoire of May 17, 1939</hi></head>
                <p>The Chinese courts in the International Settlement do not now try anti-Japanese
                    terrorists. In other criminal cases where Japanese are complainants, these
                    courts have invariably rendered decisions without prejudice and no complaint has
                    been heard in regard to decisions in Sino-Japanese civil cases.</p>
                <p>The American Government contemplates releasing immediately to the press the text
                    of this <hi rendition="#italic">aide mémoire</hi>.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-17">May 17, 1939</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
